From 232b8db9cba90ffa7ee515a64c65ad3bd458eb73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:17:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: four ranks on a ring: the RoCE all-gather with
 neighbours relaying (TF_ROCE_RING=1)

A sibling of roce.zig for a switchless ring of four: each rank writes its shard to both neighbours by one-shot RDMA
writes, each neighbour relays one logical half on to the rank across, the kernel waits six flags and copies the four
shards out in rank order; graph replays by the device epoch as the two-rank path. A rank posts its own sequence only
after its relays of the previous one are posted and completed. Opt-in: TF_ROCE=1 TF_ROCE_RING=1 at world 4, with
TF_ROCE_HCA naming the device toward the previous rank then the one toward the next; any rank that cannot bring it up
puts all four back on NCCL. tf-cuda-test roce-ring <rank> checks bytes against NCCL, graph replays and times a call.
roce.zig's verbs ABI, HCA naming and GID lookup become pub for the sibling.
